ncumbency": 0.0, "money": 1.55}, "rating_margin": 12.0, "sigma_race": 5.5, "sigma_total": 5.91, "baseline_margin": 9.6, "analyst_adjustment": -0.6, "key_factors": ["Klobuchar's statewide name recognition and roughly 20-to-1 fundraising edge over Demuth", "Minnesota's Democratic lean and a favorable 2026 environment for the party", "Consensus Likely/Solid D expert ratings and prediction markets near 95%", "September polling tightening and a $10 million pro-Demuth PAC infusion"], "rationale": "Klobuchar leads the polling average by high single digits and holds a dominant money and name-recognition advantage in a Democratic-leaning state, while raters across the spectrum call the race Likely or Solid D and markets price her near 95%. Modest late-summer tightening and new Republican outside money argue for Likely rather than Safe.", "watch": "The October 21 debate and whether the $10 million Demuth-aligned PAC spending pulls polls toward the low single digits shown in the most recent Republican-leaning survey.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Open seat: Tim Walz (D) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Minnesota's governorship is open with Tim Walz retiring, and Democrats have turned to Senator Amy Klobuchar while Lisa Demuth heads the Republican ticket. Polling since mid-summer consistently shows Klobuchar ahead, though the gap has narrowed from double digits in August to high single digits in September, with one Republican-leaning survey showing just a two-point race. Klobuchar holds an overwhelming financial advantage, raising roughly twenty times what Demuth has, but a Demuth-aligned committee recently received a $10 million infusion in what has become the most expensive governor's race in state history.\n\nRaters across the spectrum call the race Likely or Solid Democratic, and prediction markets put Klobuchar's chances around 93 to 95 percent. Minnesota's Democratic-leaning electorate and a favorable environment underpin her position, but the outside spending and a scheduled October 21 debate give Republicans chances to test the race. A minor-party candidate registers negligible support.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9683, "margin": 10.03}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9647, "margin": 9.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.931, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9507, "margin": 8.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9476, "margin": 9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.9456, "margin": 9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.9491, "margin": 9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.9656, "margin": 9.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.9546, "margin": 9.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.9536, "margin": 9.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.9443, "margin": 8.8}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.9456, "margin": 9.0}]}